  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rohingya Humanitarian Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2017 over 700,000 refugees crossed the border into Bangladesh creating one of the world&#x2019;s largest humanitarian crisis. This population is living alongside host communities in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar and is dependent on the provision of humanitarian assistance to meet daily needs including food, shelter, health and protection.  In alignment with Australia&#x2019;s humanitarian priorities, this investment will support high performing existing partners to provide life-saving assistance, protection services for women and children, and to increase the resilience of the Rohingya population and host communities in Bangladesh. The total estimated value of this investment is $24.3 million to be expensed during the 2018-2019 financial year.</narrative>
  </description>
